## Development Approach

This project follows an incremental development approach.

Instead of creating every service and technology at the beginning, each component is introduced when it solves a specific business or engineering requirement.

Examples:

- Kafka for asynchronous event-driven communication
- Redis for caching and performance improvement
- Oracle for transactional operational data
- Snowflake for analytics and reporting
- Spring Batch for large-volume file processing
- AWS S3 for file storage
- Resilience4j for fault tolerance
- Kubernetes for container orchestration
- Terraform for infrastructure provisioning
- Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring

## Git Branching Strategy

The project follows a simple professional branching model:

- `main` — stable or production-ready code
- `develop` — integration branch
- `feature/*` — individual development work

Feature development is completed in a feature branch and merged into `develop` through a Pull Request.

Stable releases will eventually be promoted from `develop` to `main`.

## Development Roadmap

### Phase 1 — Foundation
Environment setup, repository structure, Spring Boot setup, API standards, Git workflow, project architecture.

### Phase 2 — Customer Management
Customer domain, DTOs, service layer, repository layer, Oracle integration, validation, exception handling, CRUD APIs, testing.

### Phase 3 — Account and Transaction Services
Account management, transaction workflows, service communication, financial processing.

### Phase 4 — Security
Spring Security, JWT, OAuth 2.0, authentication, authorization, RBAC.

### Phase 5 — Event-Driven Architecture
Kafka producers, consumers, event design, retries, dead-letter handling, idempotency.

### Phase 6 — Batch Processing
Spring Batch, file ingestion, chunk processing, validation, retries, skip handling, batch monitoring.

### Phase 7 — AWS File Integration
Amazon S3 and cloud-based file handling.

### Phase 8 — Analytics
Snowflake integration, reporting and analytical workloads.

### Phase 9 — Frontend
Angular application, customer screens, account screens, transaction screens and dashboards.

### Phase 10 — Performance and Resiliency
Redis caching, circuit breakers, retries, rate limiting, timeout handling.

### Phase 11 — Containers and Kubernetes
Docker, Docker Compose, Kubernetes deployments, services, configuration and secrets.

### Phase 12 — AWS Deployment
EKS, ECR, MSK, IAM, networking, Secrets Manager, CloudWatch and load balancing.

### Phase 13 — CI/CD and Infrastructure
GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Terraform and automated deployments.

### Phase 14 — Production Readiness
Observability, centralized logging, tracing, performance testing, security review, integration testing and production hardening.

